# Accepted base-image vulnerabilities (Trivy).
#
# These CVEs are all in Node's own bundled npm distribution that ships inside
# the `node:24-alpine` base image under
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/ (brace-expansion, ip-address,
# tar, undici). They are:
#   - NOT part of the application dependency tree: `npm audit --omit=dev` and a
#     Trivy scan of the lockfile report 0 findings for the app's production deps.
#   - NOT reachable at runtime: the app starts with `node dist/boot.js` and never
#     invokes npm's bundled CLI modules with untrusted input.
#   - NOT resolvable upstream today: the latest npm still bundles vulnerable
#     brace-expansion@5.0.7 (fix 5.0.9) and ip-address@10.2.0 (fix 10.3.1).
#
# Revisit on every Node/npm minor update and remove entries that the updated
# base image has fixed.
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
CVE-2026-69192
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874
CVE-2026-12151
